  "id": "COMPOUND:22618 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc141945 and SF-188 through a series of target interactions involving microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol, Amurensin, and CID 11603911, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of SF-188. The consistent presence of microtubule-associated protein 1B as a common target across these compounds indicates a possible mechanism of action involving this protein. The evidence supports a pathway where Npc141945 may influence the expression or activity of microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn could be targeted by these compounds to reach SF-188. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of microtubule-associated protein 1B as a central node in the interaction network between Npc141945 and SF-188.",
